{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.CategoricalDqSquared","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.CategoricalDqSquared","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Instanton","lean:module:QOU.GroundRingCore","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.categorical_dq_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.categorical_dq_squared","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalDqSquared.lean#L100-L127","doc":"**Proposition (Non-vanishing of d_q²).**\nThe composition `d_q ∘ d_q : Ωᵏ(A) → Ωᵏ⁺²(A)` does not vanish\nfor generic forms when `q ≠ 1`:\n`d_q² α = q⁻¹(1 − q⁻¹) ω_V ∧_q [ξ, α]`.\n\n`d_q² = 0` iff `q = 1` (classical) or `[ξ, α] = 0` (ξ-invariant forms).\n\nWe prove the classical direction: when `q = 1` and `d² = 0`, then `d_q² = 0`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:categorical-dq-squared}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:categorical-dq-squared","label":"prop:categorical-dq-squared","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared.md"},{"@id":"block:prf:categorical-dq-squared","label":"prf:categorical-dq-squared","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-dq-squared-proof.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_sq_eq_zero_of_scalar_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_sq_eq_zero_of_scalar_one","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/CategoricalDqSquared.lean#L80-L98","doc":"**Scalar-generic core of `d_q² = 0` at `q = 1`** (pre-archimedean, §7c).\n\nIn the `.md` notation `a = q⁻¹`, `b = 1 - q⁻¹`, the q-exterior\nderivative is `d_q = a·d + b·(π_V ≫ d)`.  The classical-limit\nvanishing uses no property of the scalar ring beyond `1 - 1 = 0`:\n`a = 1` forces `b = 0`, hence `d_q = d` and `d_q ≫ d_q = d ≫ d = 0`.\n\nStated over an arbitrary ring `R` and an `R`-linear preadditive\ncategory, so the argument is available over the Laurent ground ring\n`R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` above.  `Ring` is the weakest class that admits the\nconstruction: `CategoryTheory.Linear` needs a `Semiring`, and the\ncoefficient `1 - a` needs subtraction; commutativity is never used. ","signatureChunk":0}]}